// Test: bugfixes/codegen_void_call_with_any_dest_no_store
// Grammar: expression_statement, function_call
// Semantic: SEM020 (call resolution), COM001 (WASM validation)
//
// Regression pin for the COM001 family recorded locally on 0.33.23 as
// fingerprint a97c328ab0393810 (+ 10 related fingerprints, all with the
// same offset pattern near func[234]).
//
// The MIR builder assigns a temporary `dest` (Any-typed) to expression-
// statement calls like `server.sleep(0)`. In the codegen path for
// has_dest=true + wasm_return_mir=None + dest_type=Any, `store_to_local`
// was called unconditionally — but the WASM call left nothing on the
// stack because the bridge signature is `(i64) -> void`. That produced
// COM001 "expected i32 but nothing on stack" at validation time.
//
// Fix: check `is_known_void_by_name` OR the hardcoded void-builtin list
// before storing, and skip the store if the call is void. See
// src/codegen/mir_codegen/instructions.rs (the Any-dest branch inside
// the has_dest+no-signature path).
//
// This test just calls `server.sleep(0)` at start-block level — the
// exact 3-line shape that reproduced the bug on 0.33.55.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.56
// Expected output:
//   ok

start:
	server.sleep(0)
	printl("ok")
